{# Reference-runtime configuration.  Thread-id ranges follow the per-node
   width.  The pthread binding line pins one thread per CPU, absolute ids
   0..width-1 — valid wherever a rank owns its host (one rank per node, or a
   single local rank).  When local ranks share a host, the numa BLOCK policy
   shifts each rank's block by its own MPI rank (cpu = offset + width *
   (rank % ranks)) inside the runtime, so one file serves every rank.  The
   binding value must stay a single lo-hi range (the parser silently unbinds
   trailing threads on any CSV form), the numa policy must stay BLOCK (RR
   divides by ranks-1: SIGFPE at one rank), and the numa key must never
   render without its complete value (the parser SEGVs on a bare key). #}
